<title>FRANCE: FRENCH ELECTION - Latest projections at 1800 GMT.</title>
<headline>FRENCH ELECTION - Latest projections at 1800 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the latest projections by private polling institutes after the decisive second round of France's election for the 577-seat National Assembly, held on Sunday.</p>
<p>A total of 289 seats is required for an absolute majority.</p>
<p>The projections are based on actual votes counted in sample constituencies.</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> PROJECTED SEATS	     BVA	   SOFRES	  CSA</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		    36	     36	     35</p>
<p> Socialists+allies	  290	    289	    298</p>
<p> Ecologists		     8		8		8</p>
<p> RPR-UDF+allies	     242	    243	    242</p>
<p> National Front		 1		1		2</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>BVA polls broadcast by France 2 television and Europe 1 radio SOFRES polls broadcast by TF1 television and RTL radio CSA polls broadcast by France 3 television and Radio France</p>
</text>
